### UrbanHat API - Flujo de roles (REST Client)
### Ejecuta cada bloque con "Send Request" en VS Code.
### Requiere tener corriendo: npm run dev

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/v1

### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### Variables (ajusta si cambiaste tu .env.local)
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

@seedKey = superadminseedkey123
@superadminEmail = superadmin@test.com
@superadminPassword = superadmin123

@sellerName = Seller Demo
@sellerEmail = seller1@test.com
@sellerPassword = seller123
@sellerShop = Caps Norte

### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 1) Seed de superadmin (solo una vez)
### Crea el superadmin si no existe.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/seed-superadmin
x-seed-key: {{seedKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 2) Login superadmin
### Obtiene token JWT + cookie. Usaremos token para requests API.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

# @name loginSuperadmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{superadminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{superadminPassword}}"
}

### Token del superadmin (se toma del response anterior)
@superadminToken = {{loginSuperadmin.response.body.$.data.token}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 3) Ver perfil autenticado (superadmin)
### Debe regresar role: "superadmin"
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{superadminToken}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 4) Crear seller (solo superadmin)
### Este endpoint NO lo puede usar buyer/seller normal.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

# @name createSeller
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/sellers
Authorization: Bearer {{superadminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "{{sellerName}}",
  "email": "{{sellerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{sellerPassword}}",
  "shopName": "{{sellerShop}}"
}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 5) Login seller
### Obtiene token JWT del seller para su dashboard/API.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

# @name loginSeller
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{sellerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{sellerPassword}}"
}

@sellerToken = {{loginSeller.response.body.$.data.token}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 6) Ver perfil autenticado (seller)
### Debe regresar role: "seller"
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 7) Seller crea producto
### Solo seller puede crear productos.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

# @name createProductAsSeller
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Gorra Demo Seller",
  "description": "Producto creado por seller vía API",
  "price": 499,
  "stock": 12,
  "imageUrl": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/image/upload/sample.jpg",
  "category": "Snapback"
}

@productId = {{createProductAsSeller.response.body.$.data.id}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 8) Seller lista sus productos (mine=true)
### Solo trae productos del seller autenticado.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

GET {{baseUrl}}/products?mine=true
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 9) Seller actualiza su producto
### Si intenta actualizar producto de otro seller, debe fallar.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 549,
  "stock": 10
}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 10) Seller elimina su producto (soft delete)
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 11) Superadmin lista usuarios
### Debe incluir superadmin/seller/buyer (sin password).
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{superadminToken}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 12) Cambio de contraseña (usuario autenticado)
### Puede usarlo superadmin o seller con su propio token.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{superadminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "{{superadminPassword}}",
  "newPassword": "superadmin1234"
}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 13) Register buyer (público)
### Registro normal de comprador para app móvil/web.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

# @name registerBuyer
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Buyer Demo",
  "email": "buyer1@test.com",
  "password": "buyer123"
}

@buyerToken = {{registerBuyer.response.body.$.data.token}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### 14) Buyer guarda dirección de envío en DB
### Persistencia real de dirección en MongoDB.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------

PUT {{baseUrl}}/account/address
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "direccion": "Calle Principal 123",
  "ciudad": "Monterrey",
  "estado": "Nuevo Leon",
  "codigoPostal": "64000",
  "telefono": "8112345678"
}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------
### Notas rápidas
### - Si seed devuelve created:false, significa que superadmin ya existe (correcto).
### - Si falla seed con 401, revisa ADMIN_SEED_KEY en .env.local (sin espacios).
### - Para Cloudinary, en imageUrl usa la URL pública segura que te devuelve Cloudinary.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------
